\cf0 \
The fixed 0.5 threshold is another limitation. In the report's test results, HGB found 50 more positive cases than Logistic Regression, with 33 more false positives, but still missed about 41% of actual positive cases. A useful next step would be to select a threshold from training or out-of-fold predictions based on an explicit recall or error-cost requirement, without using the test set to choose it. I consider the fixed threshold acceptable for this report because no task-specific cost or recall target was supplied.\
\
\

\f0\b 3. Trustworthiness\

\f1\b0 \
I used reviews from ChatGPT and Gemini as secondary checks on clarity, internal consistency, and assignment alignment. I did not treat them as independent verification of the data or results. I also used Colab to inspect the data and cross-check class balance, correlations, AP, precision, recall, and F1.\
